This distribution is not source-only: mzLibRust drives, and is intended to be shipped
alongside, compiled third-party software so that using it requires nothing but cargo.
What follows is the required attribution for everything in that payload. It mirrors
pyMzLib's NOTICE, because both bindings carry the same bridge.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mzLib  -  LGPL-3.0-or-later
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mzLibRust redistributes mzLib in compiled form, inside the `mzlib-bridge` executable.

  Source:  https://github.com/smith-chem-wisc/mzLib
  Commit:  reported at runtime by mzlib::bridge_version()

Your rights under LGPL-3.0 section 4 include modifying the mzLib portion of this work
and relinking it. Two things are done deliberately to keep that practical rather than
theoretical:

  1. The bridge is published WITHOUT trimming and WITHOUT ReadyToRun compilation
     (see pyMzLib's pkg/build/publish-bridge.ps1). The mzLib assemblies therefore
     remain as ordinary, replaceable IL inside the single-file bundle rather than
     being merged or ahead-of-time compiled into it.

  2. The complete source of mzLibRust and of the bridge is public, and the
     MZLIB_BRIDGE environment variable lets any user point this crate at a bridge
     they built themselves from a modified mzLib — no rebuild of this crate required.
     That variable is a licence affordance as much as a development convenience.

